From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WLTB Gino <gino@wltb.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ingenic-sdk: gc4023 t41: add the real 30fps mode

The t41 port's win_sizes[0] claims "2560x1440 @max 30fps" but points at
the 25fps register table (VTS 1875), and SENSOR_SUPPORT_30FPS_SCLK is
computed from the never-shipped 30fps table (2025*1200*2*25). Booting
[0] yields 25fps; any runtime fps request computes a garbage VTS from
the bogus constant.

The t32 sibling already carries the true table (mipi 864Mbps/lane, PLL
0x0a36=0x60, 0x061d/e=0x22/0x78, VTS 0x05dc=1500) and its set_fps
arithmetic is self-consistent. Port that table, aim win_sizes[0] at it,
raise the declared mipi clk to 864, and set the SCLK macros to the real
pixel clock: hts*vts*fps = 1200*1800*25 = 54e6 reproduces the shipped
25fps (VTS 1800) and 20fps (VTS 2250) tables exactly, and gives
VTS 1500 = 30fps for the new table.

T41NQ boards with GC4023 (Noorio T110) now boot at 30fps and honor fps
changes.

Signed-off-by: WLTB Gino <gino@wltb.local>
---
--- a/4.4.94/sensor-src/t41/gc4023.c
+++ b/4.4.94/sensor-src/t41/gc4023.c
@@ -32,8 +32,8 @@
 #define SENSOR_REG_END 0xffff
 #define SENSOR_REG_DELAY 0x0000
 #define SENSOR_REG_DELAY 0x0000
-#define SENSOR_SUPPORT_30FPS_SCLK (0x7e9 * 0x4b0 * 2 * 25)
-#define SENSOR_SUPPORT_20FPS_SCLK 108*1000*1000
+#define SENSOR_SUPPORT_30FPS_SCLK (0x4b0 * 0x708 * 25)
+#define SENSOR_SUPPORT_20FPS_SCLK (0x4b0 * 0x8ca * 20)
 #define SENSOR_OUTPUT_MIN_FPS 5
 #define SENSOR_VERSION "H20230720"
